GreenFrame is an unofficial add-on for SmoovPlay (https://github.com/smoovplay/smoovplay), Copyright (c) 2026 the
SmoovPlay authors, MIT License. SmoovPlay must be installed separately; it does all of the decoding, frame
generation, upscaling and display. GreenFrame uses from SmoovPlay:

  * SmoovPlay's frame tap: the shared-memory interface ("Local\smoovplay-tap") and compressed-frame layout that
    SmoovPlay designed and documents for other apps, read by SmoovPlay's run.py --source tap.
  * SmoovPlay's frame-tap writer class (framegen.chiaki_tap.FrameTap), imported at run time from the user's own
    SmoovPlay installation; not copied into GreenFrame.
  * SmoovPlay's bundled Python runtime, which runs GreenFrame's bridge.
  * One adapted function: nal_units() in bridge/greenframe_bridge.py is adapted from nal_units() in SmoovPlay's
    framegen/chiaki_tap.py. SmoovPlay's MIT License and copyright notice: licenses/SmoovPlay-LICENSE.txt.

SmoovPlay in turn builds on chiaki-ng (AGPL-3.0), RIFE (hzwer's Practical-RIFE and HolyWu's vs-rife, MIT),
AMD FidelityFX Super Resolution 1.0 (MIT) and others listed in SmoovPlay's THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt. None of
these are included in GreenFrame.

Release builds bundle Electron (https://www.electronjs.org/, MIT License) and Chromium; their licenses ship in
the release folder (LICENSE, LICENSES.chromium.html).

